{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "3b3a9b55-6b1e-4e2f-8d46-4b9c7a0f2e51",
    "name": "SMS REST API - v2",
    "description": "## SMS REST API v2\n\n### Variables\n- `base_url` — e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:8000`\n- `api_token` — set automatically by **Login** test when `data.api_token` is present\n- `pin_code` — OTP code used in Login step 2\n\n### Login\n- Two-step login flow:\n  - Step 1: send `user_name` + `user_pass` without `pin_code` → response `code=1002` (`otp_required=true`).\n  - Step 2: send the same credentials with `pin_code` → response `code=1001` with `api_token`.\n- Optional body field `force_new_token` (boolean): if omitted, an existing `api_token` may be **reused** (`reused: true` in response).\n- The API service must be enabled on the account (error 1401 otherwise).\n\n### Account\n- `GET .../me` returns: `user_no`, `user_name`, `prev`, `name`, `email`, `company`, `mobile`, `public_ip`, `credits`, `due_amount`, `finish_date`.\n- `GET .../credits` returns `{ data: { credits } }`.\n- Legacy alias still exists: `.../account/credits`.\n\n### Sender names\n- `GET .../senders` — approved names on the account (`user.sender`).\n- `GET .../senders/requests` — this account's requests (`send_no`, status, `has_attachment`).\n- `POST .../senders` — `multipart/form-data`: `sender_name`, `authorized_name`, `company_name`, `mobile`, optional `notes`, optional `attachment` (PDF/JPG/PNG, max 10 MB). Returns `data.send_no`.\n- `POST .../senders/{send_no}/authorization` — upload or replace the letter. Use `send_no` from the add response or from the requests list.\n- The file is stored in the portal `auth_letter` folder as `{send_no}.{ext}` and `send_auth` is set to 1.\n\n### Token formats\n- `Authorization: Bearer <api_token>`\n- `X-API-TOKEN: <api_token>`\n- `api_token` query/body parameter\n\n### Send message\n`POST .../messages/send` — requires `sender`; success: `data.provider` = `queue_sms`, `data.provider_response` includes `networks_report`, `total_cost`, `sms_refs`, `filter_flag`, `filtered`.\n\n### Send message summary\nSame body as send, but only returns routing, segments, cost, and `can_send` without sending or deducting credits.\n\n### Send group\n`POST .../messages/sendgroup` — requires `group_ids`, `message`, `sender`; loads contacts from selected groups, normalizes mobiles, removes duplicates, then sends through the same pipeline.\n\n### Send group summary\nSame body as sendgroup, but only returns recipients, cost, and `can_send` without sending or deducting credits.\n\n### Send variables\n`POST .../messages/sendvar` — requires `sender_id`; template + `rows`.\n\n### Send variables summary\nSame body as sendvar, but only returns rows summary, total segments, total cost, and `can_send` without sending or deducting credits.\n\n### Archive message\n`POST .../messages/archive` — archive-only: stores the message in the sent history (`smsc_sent`) without deducting credits and without queuing/sending. Requires `mobile`, `message`, approved `sender`, and `sms_type` (currently only `300` = WhatsApp text message).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000" },
    { "key": "api_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "pin_code", "value": "" },
    { "key": "send_no", "value": "18451" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth (REST v2)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (REST v2 Step 1/2) - saves api_token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "try {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  const token = json?.data?.api_token;",
                  "  if (token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('api_token', token);",
                  "  }",
                  "} catch (e) {}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"user_name\": \"demo\",\n  \"user_pass\": \"demo\",\n  \"pin_code\": \"{{pin_code}}\",\n  \"force_new_token\": false\n}"
            },
            "description": "Step 1: leave `pin_code` empty to receive OTP challenge (`code=1002`). Step 2: set `pin_code` to received OTP to get `api_token` (`code=1001`). Set `force_new_token=true` to always issue a fresh token.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/rest/v2/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "rest", "v2", "auth", "login"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout (REST v2)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{api_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/rest/v2/auth/logout",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "rest", "v2", "auth", "logout"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Send OTP (REST v2)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{api_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"sender\": \"MyBrand\",\n  \"mobile\": \"970599999999\",\n  \"msg_prefix\": \"Your verification code is\",\n  \"exp_min\": 10\n}"
            },
            "description": "Token-protected OTP sender. Sends a one-time verification code by SMS to the given mobile number; the code is kept temporarily so it can be checked later via the Verify OTP request.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/rest/v2/auth/otp/send",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "rest", "v2", "auth", "otp", "send"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify OTP (REST v2)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{api_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"sender\": \"MyBrand\",\n  \"mobile\": \"970599999999\",\n  \"otp\": \"123456\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Verifies the OTP code previously sent to the same sender and mobile. Once verified successfully, the code is consumed and cannot be used again.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/rest/v2/auth/otp/verify",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "rest", "v2", "auth", "otp", "verify"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
